course: dictionary
lesson: 9975
title: Teamwork
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Teamwork means working together well as a group to reach a shared goal, with each person helping the others. Think of a football team or a class project: everyone has a job, and the team wins or finishes only if they help each other.
explain: Teamwork is uncountable, like water or happiness. You do not say «a teamwork» or «teamworks». You say «good teamwork» or «great teamwork». The word can be used alone, as in «Teamwork makes the dream work».
explain: Good teamwork has clear signs. People share the jobs, they listen to each other, and they help when someone is stuck. In a story, a small group that uses teamwork can beat a stronger enemy, so the word often shows the hero's secret weapon.
fact: Teamwork means working together well as a group to reach a shared goal.
fact: Teachers praise teamwork in PE, group projects and science experiments, when people share jobs, listen and help.
fact: «Teamwork» is uncountable, so say «good teamwork», not «teamworks».
fact: «Ant colonies do amazing teamwork with no boss, each ant following simple rules.»
fact: «Lionesses do most of the hunting together», which is teamwork in the wild.
exercise: In «Ant colonies do amazing teamwork with no boss», what does teamwork mean? | Working alone without asking anyone for help | Having one boss who tells everyone what to do | *Working together well as a group to reach a shared goal | Playing a game against each other
exercise: Teachers praise «good teamwork» in PE. Which example shows good teamwork? | *Sharing the jobs and listening to each other | Doing your own work and ignoring the group | Shouting at others when they make a mistake | Grabbing the ball and never passing it
exercise: Which phrase uses «teamwork» correctly? | a great teamworks | *great teamwork | teamworks are great | many teamworks
test: «Research on games is mixed: some may help with problem-solving or teamwork.» What might some games help with? | Lying down all day | Doing more homework at midnight | Sleeping for longer | *Problem-solving or teamwork
test: Maya and Sam split the jobs for their science project, and each one listens to the other's ideas. What is this an example of? | *Teamwork | Giving up | Showing off | Keeping secrets
exam: In a story, a small group of friends beats a stronger enemy by sharing jobs and helping each other. Which word best describes what they used? | *Teamwork | Luck alone | Fear | Shouting
